Verb-gloss harmonization: format 1 ("to eat, drink, dance") -> format 2 ("to eat, to drink, to dance").
Swept 2026-07-26.

How the candidates were found: split each english gloss on ";" then " - " then "," (commas
inside parentheses do not split), ignoring a leading qualifier like "(idiom)"/"(slang)".
A card is a candidate when one segment in a comma run starts with "to " and another does not.
That gave 329 candidates; the list below is the 56 where the bare segment is genuinely a verb.
The other 273 were rejected because the bare segment is an adjective ("to stand out, outstanding"),
a noun ("thief, to steal"), or an adverb ("to repeat, repeatedly, again").

Mark any line you disagree with. Nothing has been applied yet.

Note: 47 of the 56 also carry an example "meaning" label that copies the gloss verbatim;
those labels will be updated to match. All 56 need their english word clip regenerated.

